<pre class="lang-dart prettyprint-override"><code>class A {}

class B {
  final A objOfA;
  const B(this.objOfA);
}

mixin MixedA on A {
  void someNewMethod() {
    // do something
  }
}

mixin MixedB on B {
  void someMethod() {
    objOfA.someNewMethod(); // &lt;-- error
  }
}
</code></pre>,"<p><code>mixin MixedB on B</code> means that classes that use <code>MixedB</code> are known only to derive from <code>B</code>.  Class <code>B</code> provides no guarantee that its <code>objOfA</code> member is an instance of <code>MixedA</code>.  Some of your options:</p>

